  My following comments are meant to be helpful, not just criticism for
the sake of it.  They may seem like small points individually, but put
them all together and they make a big difference in the game.

>
>Just to follow up on my post, here's how I'm doing now. After those 78
>straight YASD's and a cry for help in this ng, I've played 2 games that
>ended me geing dead, but those were very promising games and they were
>"good deaths". The third game is still on and looking good.
>
>This is me just entering Gehennom.
>
>Welho the Sorcerer        St:18 Dx:18 Co:16 In:25 Wi:23 Ch:10  Chaotic
>Dlvl:25 $:0  HP:211(211) Pw:235(235) AC:-21 Exp:18 T:49600 Burdened

  - Don't be burdened!  With the Eye's portal capability going to a
stash is quick and easy.  Shrinks the dungeon down tremendously.
#invoking the Eye lets you travel instantaneously to any other dungeon
branch you've already visited.  "If you die with the Eye you deserve
it."  Branches include: Dungeons of Doom, Gnomish Mines, Sokoban, Ft.
Ludios, Gehennom (start with the VotD), Vlad's.

  - Be fast, if not very fast.  Spell of haste self is perfect for a
wizard.  Just keep casting it when you slow down.  That lets you wear
whatever boots you like. (I prefer the guaranteed water walking boots in
Vlads.)

  - Since you're at XL:18 you have intrinsic teleport control.  Get
teleportitis and teleport with ^T.  Add those to magic mapping and
Gehennom's a breeze.  You can also save mana by waiting for the random
teleports to kick in.

  A +1 ring of increase strength will add one point of damage to your
weapon hits.  This is where playing a human is better than playing an
elven wizard.  There are so many useful spells you could better be
casting than attack spells.  A human with Str:18/** gets +6 damage bonus
per hit.  Averaging 2x daggers per fling at Expert and that's +12 damage
right there.

  - Improve your Cha and dance with foocubi for XL.  Maximizing Cha
gives a better chance of keeping the HoB on.  Mana increases during
level gains will be improved thereby.  

  - The spells of magic missile and cone of cold do damage based on XL.
At XL:30 magic missile averages 58 points of damage per hit per monster.
So does Cone of Cold.  At Skilled+ Cone of Cold hits a 3x3 grid an
average of 4 times.

