>
> Amulets
> f - the blessed Eye of the Aethiopica (being worn)
> E - an uncursed amulet of life saving

  Wear the "oLifeSaving instead of the Eye of Aethiopica.  All that
wearing the Eye gives you is ESP.  Just be sure to carry it in open
inventory.  Skilled+ spell of detect monsters will show all monsters on
the entire level for an extended period of time.

  Yes, just having the Eye in open inventory will grant MR and fast mana
regeneration.

> Weapons
> a - the blessed rustproof +2 Magicbane (weapon in hand)

  Enchant Magicbane to +6/7.  You'll never go back once you do.  Even
the spoiler says Magicbane does more damage at maximum enchantment.  At
+7 it will do 4 more points of damage per hit.  What would you give for
a +4 ring of increase damage?  A ring that doesn't have a nutrition cost
and doesn't take up a ring slot?  That's what maximum enchanting of
Magicbane gives you.  If you don't want to do damage you're better off
leaving Magicbane at +0 for the special probe effect.

> d - 20 blessed rustproof +4 daggers (in quiver)

  #adjust to 'Q' for easy requivering: 'QQ'.  I also hope you have
autoquiver turned on.  Use the 'f' command instead of 't' to take
advantage of autoquivering.

> Armor
> A - a blessed +3 silver dragon scale mail (being worn)
> B - a blessed fireproof +4 pair of speed boots (being worn)

  Speed boots are a generally a waste for a late game wizard.  The spell
of Haste Self gives you the very fast of speed boots.  Water walking is
better for general dungeon crawling.  (Other boots make me walk into
water. :)  Jumping boots are better for the Astral Plane.  #jumping and
Haste Self lets you travel 3x as fast as just speed boots.

  Expert spell of jumping combined with Haste Self lets you jump four
squares in a straight line.  That's traveling FOUR times as fast as just
speed boots.  

> C - a blessed fireproof +4 cloak of magic resistance (being worn)
> G - a blessed fireproof +2 pair of leather gloves (being worn)
> H - a blessed rustproof +5 helm of brilliance (being worn)
>[...]

  Where's your enchanted small shield?  You'll find plenty of small
shields at the Castle (or Ft. Ludios).  Finding a +3 small shield is
almost guaranteed.  Fireproof it with c?oDestroyArmor.  A small shield
won't hurt your spell casting if you're at max skills and XL:30.

>
>Weapon Skills
>   #  dagger             [Expert]
>[...]
>      quarterstaff       [Skilled]

  That was a waste of two skill slots, which it looks like you need.
Those two skill slots only gave you one additional point of damage per
hit.  You could make up for not having that by dumping the quarterstaff
and wearing a shield.  (You can't wear a shield while using a
quarterstaff.)

>[...]
> Spellcasting Skills
>    #  attack spells      [Expert]

  Taking attack spells to Expert isn't critical.  Skilled is only
important if you have the spell of cone of cold.  It's generally better
to spread out enhancements to other spell schools.  There are a lot of
useful non-attack spells.  Learn to conserve mana for those spells by
using thrown Expert daggers instead of attack spells.

>       healing spells     [Basic]
>    *  divination spells  [Skilled]
>       enchantment spells [Basic]
>    #  clerical spells    [Skilled]
>       escape spells      [Unskilled]
>       matter spells      [Unskilled]

  Once you get the Eye of Aethiopica you should cast a spell every time
you're at max mana.  Just for practice if nothing else.  That's also a
good time to study up on the effects of the spells.

  E.g. matter spells
  - Cancellation means you can dump those dangerous wands of 
      cancellation.
  - Spell of polymorph is like an unlimited wand of wishing.  (I usually
    end up with a vanity stack of 10 blessed +7 silver daggers named 
    SilverStorm.)
  - The spell of dig is also nice.

  Escape spells:
  - The spell of jump triples your traveling speed on no-teleport 
    levels.  Great for escape.
  - The spell of levitation is great when at skilled+: controllable.
  - Haste Self gives you the very fast of speed boots and thereby frees 
    up the boot slots for more useful footgear.

  Enchantment:  XL:30 expert spell of charm monster is as close to an
instawin as you'll find.


